Modifications made by this overlay
----------------------------------

All upstream source files are used unmodified on disk. Upstream files are changed
only at build time, by the patch series in linux/patches/ applied to a fresh
checkout of the pinned upstream tag:

- 0001-desktop-linux-target.patch — adds `linux-x64` as a build target to
  upstream's desktop packaging scripts, wires the Linux unsigned/local packaging
  path, and keeps upstream's macOS/Windows signing and upload behaviour unchanged.
- 0002-brand-window-title.patch — adds the opt-in `DSH_LINUX_CLIENT_TITLE`
  selector so the unsigned/local client profile can use the official client
  window title instead of the local-build title.

Additional files in this repository, not present upstream:

- linux/electron-builder.config.mjs — Linux electron-builder wrapper that reuses
  upstream's config factory and adds AppImage, deb, rpm, and pacman targets,
  desktop metadata (`desktopName`, `syncDesktopName`, icon set), and the fpm
  package dependencies.
- linux/build/build.sh — prepares the upstream Linux tree and packages the four
  release formats.
- linux/assets/icons/ — application icons rendered from the upstream product
  icon for standard hicolor sizes.
- linux/lib/ and linux/scripts/ — release naming, SHA-256 checksums, the
  linux-update.json manifest, signing/verification, patch application, upstream
  sync decisions, and the container install tests.
- .github/workflows/build-linux.yml and .github/workflows/sync-upstream.yml —
  CI that builds, tests, signs, and publishes Linux releases and follows upstream
  `latest`.
- dsh-linux-pubkey.asc — the public key that verifies release metadata
  signatures.
- README.md, docs/, and this NOTICE.

